@startuml
title Future Migration - Idempotency Tx-A / Tx-B / Tx-C with Relational Access

autonumber
skinparam shadowing false

actor "Idempotency Executor / Integration" as IDEM
participant "TransactionExecutor" as TX
participant "JdbcIdempotencyStorage\n(future Relational-based)" as Storage
participant "RelationalTemplate" as RT
participant "SpringTransactionAwareConnectionProvider" as SCP
participant "Business / MyBatis" as Biz
database Database as DB

== Tx-A: acquire state must commit before business callback ==
IDEM -> TX : execute(REQUIRES_NEW, state-tx)
TX -> TX : begin Tx-A / bind Connection-A
TX -> Storage : tryAcquire()
Storage -> RT : update(INSERT/CAS SQL)
RT -> SCP : acquire -> transaction-bound A
SCP --> RT : BORROWED A
RT -> DB : persist PROCESSING
TX -> DB : COMMIT Tx-A
TX --> IDEM : ACQUIRED

== Tx-B: business + markSuccess one atomic local transaction ==
IDEM -> TX : execute(REQUIRED, business-tx)
TX -> TX : begin/join Tx-B / bind Connection-B
TX -> Biz : execute real business
Biz -> DB : business SQL via MyBatis / Connection-B
TX -> Storage : markSuccess(owner, version)
Storage -> RT : update(mark-success CAS)
RT -> SCP : acquire -> transaction-bound B
SCP --> RT : BORROWED B
RT -> DB : idempotency SUCCESS SQL / same Connection-B
TX -> DB : COMMIT Tx-B atomically
TX --> IDEM : success

alt business / markSuccess fails
  TX -> DB : ROLLBACK Tx-B

  == Tx-C: persist failure in independent transaction ==
  IDEM -> TX : execute(REQUIRES_NEW, failure-state-tx)
  TX -> TX : begin Tx-C / bind Connection-C
  TX -> Storage : markFailed(...)
  Storage -> RT : update(mark-failed CAS)
  RT -> SCP : acquire -> transaction-bound C
  SCP --> RT : BORROWED C
  RT -> DB : persist FAILED
  TX -> DB : COMMIT Tx-C
end

note right of RT

RelationalTemplate never decides REQUIRED / REQUIRES_NEW.

It only executes SQL on the Connection supplied by its Provider.

end note

note right of IDEM

Current JdbcExecutionManager transaction semantics
migrate upward into transaction orchestration.

end note

@enduml
